WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.361
GitHub separates three security controls.

2
00:00:07.461 --> 00:00:13.387
AI Scan and agentic autofix are generally available;
workflow lockfiles are in preview.

3
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:20.272
AI Scan reviews pull request changes beyond existing
CodeQL coverage.

4
00:00:20.372 --> 00:00:24.463
Its findings are advisory and cannot block merges
through rulesets.

5
00:00:24.563 --> 00:00:27.395
Fork and Dependabot pull requests are excluded.

6
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:35.147
Agentic autofix takes assigned default branch alerts,
excluding pull request only findings.

7
00:00:35.247 --> 00:00:39.443
It proposes changes, rechecks, and opens a draft pull
request.

8
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.844
Validation has limits, especially for custom queries
and third party alerts.

9
00:00:45.944 --> 00:00:49.309
A passed recheck does not prove the entire application
safe.

10
00:00:49.409 --> 00:00:51.388
Review the patch and relevant tests.

11
00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.331
Lockfiles address moving dependency references.

12
00:00:56.431 --> 00:01:00.329
Onboarded workflows run locked commits, even if tags
move.

13
00:01:00.429 --> 00:01:02.365
Locked code still needs review.

14
00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:09.505
Investigate findings, verify repairs, and review
dependency commits.

15
00:01:09.605 --> 00:01:12.011
Check policies and credit budgets.

16
00:01:12.111 --> 00:01:16.500
Automation supplies evidence; people make the merge
decision.

